# group-split deploys itself from its own repo (Aspire-generated compose, like
# the trakt bot), so this upstream name is that stack's, not this repo's: its
# `web` service joins `internal` under the alias `group-split-web` and Kestrel
# listens on 8080. Only `web` is published — `api` and `keycloak` stay on the
# stack's private network and are reached server-side.
http://groupsplit.sussman.win {
    reverse_proxy group-split-web:8080
}
